#### Table 2 — CDK path-based resources (logical ID stays path-derived)

A row lands here when ALL of: no physical name (or name auto-derived from logical ID), Create/Put isn't idempotent-with-side-effect (either AWS allows duplicates, or the resource is content-versioned, or identity is composite on a stable parent with no Delete-time action), and no externally-cached AWS-allocated ID. Rename produces at worst a brief deploy gap or a regenerated AWS-side ID — no CFN conflict, no silent deletion, no consumer-visible breakage.

**AWS identity mechanism** column = the actual unique key AWS uses. **Why safe** column = why rename doesn't conflict. **Rename caveat** column = secondary effects (regenerated IDs, cascading refs) that aren't CFN errors but are observable.

